4-602.13 The following nonfood contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
A) back prep table - bottom shelf and inside drawer (food splash/debris);
B) large prep cooler - general surfaces and handles (splash/grimy buildup);
C) fridge - bottom inside (food splash);
D) fryer - sides (grease/food debris);
E) wok grill - ledge underneath and drip trays (grease/food debris);
F) small table holding spices at wok grill (splash/food debris);
G) small grill - sides and drip tray (grease buildup);   and
H) table holding small grill (grease/food debris).
Clean the aforementioned items.
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.
